{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nDiscovered from majestic-depilatory-beetle. The advisory `sweep (windows)` job deselects 47 tests through `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args`, which this bug owns. Root cause (ticket comment, Windows logs at `b4e0d01b649`): two checks read POSIX mode bits that Windows does not implement. `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py:111` rejects a key file with `st_mode & 0o077`; `infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py:266` (`_assert_private_artifact_dir`) rejects an artifact directory the same way. Windows reports files as `0o666` and directories as `0o777`, so both always refuse there.\n\nPolicy is decided on cloistered-decomposed-nymph (option 3, operator comment 2026-11-18): on Windows rebar relies on the user profile's default ACL and documents the residual risk; it does not enforce key confidentiality itself.\n\n## Approach\n\nImplement the decision exactly:\n\n- Each module gets a module constant `_POSIX_MODE_BITS = os.name != \"nt\"` with a comment naming the reason (Windows has no POSIX mode bits; the decision ticket). The mode check runs only when it is true; every other check (exists, regular file / real directory, readable, symlink refusal) is unchanged on all platforms. The constant is the test seam, so both branches are tested on POSIX CI.\n- Docs: `docs/manifest-signing.md` (key section) and `docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md` (artifact directory section) state the Windows residual risk: keys and artifacts inherit their folder's ACL; `chmod` changes only the read-only bit there; nothing checks for extra ACEs such as Users or Everyone.\n- Evidence for nymph's criterion: the `sweep (windows)` job gains a non-gating step (`continue-on-error: true`) that mints a key with rebar's own generator (`rebar._opcert_signing._generate_opcert_key`, which runs `ssh-keygen`) in `runner.temp` and prints `icacls` for the key and for a `tempfile.mkdtemp()` directory (where `keyprov.compose_signer`, `keyprov.py:67`, writes its key copy). The step carries a `mechanism-ok: ci_gate` marker naming this ticket.\n- Argfile: remove the 17 `tests/integration/test_cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py` lines, whose only failure is the directory check. The 30 op-cert lines stay deselected: after the mode check, `compose_signer` validates its key copy with `ssh-keygen -y` (`keyprov.py:131-151`), and the Windows log already shows Win32-OpenSSH rejecting such a copy, in `test_opcert_privkey_env_pop_932d.py::test_compose_still_works_after_pop` (inline key, so it skips the mode check): \"Bad permissions. Try removing permissions for user: \\\\OWNER RIGHTS (S-1-3-4)\". That is a separate cause; a new bug is filed and linked for it, and those 30 lines move to its own argfile `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` (referenced from `.github/workflows/test.yml`), so this file holds only this bug's class and is deleted once empty.\n\nPortability: the only platform branch is on `os.name`; no new POSIX-only API. No config key, env var or flag is added.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/opcert_service/keyprov.py`, `infra/scripts/cleanup_comment_echo_jira.py`\n- `tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py` (new)\n- `docs/manifest-signing.md`, `docs/comment-echo-reclaim-runbook.md`\n- `.github/workflows/test.yml` (ACL evidence step; argfile reference), `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/posix-permissions.args` (deleted), `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/openssh-key-acl.args` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\n- New tests, both branches on every platform via the constant: with it false, a `0o644` key file and a `0o755` artifact directory are accepted; with it true they are rejected with the existing messages (failure path); a non-regular key path is rejected either way.\n- The existing POSIX tests of both checks keep running unchanged. `make verify` and the integration tier pass.\n- After merge, a dispatched `sweep (windows)` run on main.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The class's root cause is recorded on this ticket with the evidence that confirmed it.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, including `tests/unit/test_windows_mode_bit_skip.py`, and `pytest -m \"integration and not live\"` passes.\n- [ ] Every line removed from `posix-permissions.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [ ] `sweep (windows)` concludes `success` on that run, and its ACL step's `icacls` output is recorded on cloistered-decomposed-nymph.\n"}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795051586338403900,"uuid":"cf39373a-83aa-447d-bc8b-0612a9e6ce3a"}